pmdocs (1.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Recommend valkyrianlabs-archive-keyring so renewed APT signing-key metadata
    reaches existing installs through upgrades (it owns
    /usr/share/keyrings/valkyrianlabs.gpg and links an unmodified
    /etc/apt/keyrings/valkyrianlabs.gpg to it). Recommends, not Depends: the
    standalone .deb must install without the repository (GitHub release assets,
    the clean-install smoke test).
  * Read optional project metadata from docs/stack.toml (title, description,
    categorized technology stack) with toml++, validate it against the shared
    contract vectors, and send it as the manifest `project` key; warn when the
    server does not acknowledge it.
  * Build-depend on libtomlplusplus-dev.

 -- Valkyrian Labs <maintainers@valkyrianlabs.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:49:43 +0000

pmdocs (1.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Always bundle and install the payload-markdown skill next to
    payload-markdown-docs.
    - Vendored in skills/payload-markdown, so every build ships it, Homebrew
      included.
    - pmdocs install skill prefers the project's node_modules/payload-markdown
      (either package name) and fails when neither copy is available.
  * Add pmdocs skill check and pmdocs skill update; installed skills carry a
    skill.json manifest. validate and plan warn on stderr when the installed
    skill is outdated.
  * pmdocs install routes imports the plugin under the package name the app
    depends on.
  * Build with vl-release; the Homebrew formula builds from the release source
    archive.

 -- Valkyrian Labs <maintainers@valkyrianlabs.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:02:14 +0000

